          <div class="question"><b>Q1. What is == vs === ?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> == value only, === value + type - Always use ===</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> Both same</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> == is better</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="d"> No difference</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q2. Flexbox vs Grid?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> Flexbox = 1D (Row OR Column), Grid = 2D (Rows AND Columns)</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> Both same</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> Flexbox = 2D, Grid = 1D</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="d"> No difference</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q3. What is Box Model?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> Content + Padding + Border + Margin</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> Only content</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> Only margin</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="d"> Only padding</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q4. CSS Specificity order?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="a"> Inline > id > class > tag</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="b"> Tag > class > id > inline</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="c"> Class > id > tag > inline</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="d"> All equal</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q5. What is DOM?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="a"> Browser turns HTML into tree of objects, JS can change it</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="b"> A CSS file</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="c"> A database</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="d"> A server</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q6. What is localStorage?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="a"> Browser storage - Saves data after refresh, 5MB</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="b"> Saves only for 1 second</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="c"> Deletes on refresh</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="d"> Server storage</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q7. Div vs Span?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="a"> div = Block, full width, new line | span = Inline, only needed width</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="b"> Both block</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="c"> Both inline</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="d"> Both same</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q8. How to answer "Tell me about yourself"?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="a"> Name + Skill + Projects + Goal - 1 minute</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="b"> Full life story 10 minutes</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="c"> "I don't know"</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="d"> Only name</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q9. What to say if you don't know answer?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="a"> "I don't know this exact thing, but I know something similar..." + Explain</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="b"> Stay silent</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="c"> "I don't know" and stop</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="d"> Lie</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q10. How to reverse string "Ali" in JS?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="a"> "Ali".split("").reverse().join("") = "ilA"</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="b"> "Ali".reverse()</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="c"> reverse("Ali")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="d"> "Ali".split()</label></div>
